<i>a new addition to the Hart Café Band.</i>

2662
02:47:36.922 --> 02:47:41.051
<i>Fresh from pictures.
Mr. Sidney Palmer on the trumpet.</i>

2663
02:47:41.385 --> 02:47:42.970
[audience applauding]

2664
02:47:49.518 --> 02:47:52.604
Hey. Sid. You want to say a few words?

2665
02:47:53.772 --> 02:47:54.815
Thank you. Tom.

2666
02:47:54.898 --> 02:47:57.985
I just would like to say to you
how happy I am to be here.

2667
02:47:58.443 --> 02:48:00.529
You all are such
a beautiful. lovely crowd.

2668
02:48:00.696 --> 02:48:01.905
So. thank you.

2669
02:48:02.197 --> 02:48:05.576
If I can. I'd like to play something
that I used to play

2670
02:48:06.159 --> 02:48:08.203
back in the days.

2671
02:48:09.162 --> 02:48:10.455
I hope you all enjoy it.

2672
02:48:12.916 --> 02:48:14.751
[melancholy music playing]

2673
02:50:03.110 --> 02:50:04.528
[melancholy music concludes]

2674
02:50:04.778 --> 02:50:06.780
[car horns honking]

2675
02:50:25.048 --> 02:50:27.634
[in Spanish] This is it.
What do you think?

2676
02:50:28.760 --> 02:50:30.220
That's where I used to work.

2677
02:50:32.806 --> 02:50:33.932
[in English] Passes. sir?

2678
02:50:34.015 --> 02:50:35.695
[in English] We're just looking.
Thank you.

2679
02:50:36.810 --> 02:50:38.478
<i>Hola. </i>Hi.

2680
02:50:38.770 --> 02:50:40.230
[in Spanish] I used to work here.

2681
02:50:40.355 --> 02:50:41.355
<i>Sí?</i>

2682
02:50:41.690 --> 02:50:42.733
A long time ago.

2683
02:50:44.109 --> 02:50:45.629
[in Spanish] I started here last year.

2684
02:50:45.694 --> 02:50:46.820
You like it?

2685
02:50:47.279 --> 02:50:48.739
- [in English] It's okay.
<i>- Sí?</i>

2686
02:50:49.448 --> 02:50:51.175
[in Spanish] They make anything good
these days?

2687
02:50:51.199 --> 02:50:52.802
[guard. in Spanish]
You don't go to the movies?

2688
02:50:52.826 --> 02:50:56.455
Not much anymore. I own an audio shop
in New York. Radios. that kind of thing.

2689
02:50:56.705 --> 02:50:57.998
- New York?
<i>- Sí.</i>

2690
02:50:59.082 --> 02:51:00.917
It's her first time in L.A.

2691
02:51:01.209 --> 02:51:02.711
- Oh yeah?
<i>- Hola.</i>

2692
02:51:02.878 --> 02:51:04.129
Nice talking to you.

2693
02:51:04.254 --> 02:51:05.839
<i>- Cuídese mucho.</i>
- You too.

2694
02:51:06.381 --> 02:51:08.091
I'm bored.

2695
02:51:09.217 --> 02:51:10.343
Really?

2696
02:51:12.345 --> 02:51:13.680
So early?

2697
02:51:14.306 --> 02:51:15.599
- Let's go.
- No. you stay.

2698
02:51:15.682 --> 02:51:17.976
I'll take her to the hotel.

2699
02:51:18.226 --> 02:51:19.478
We'll eat some ice cream.

2700
02:51:19.603 --> 02:51:20.854
[speaking Spanish]

2701
02:51:22.230 --> 02:51:23.607
<i>- Muchas gracias.</i>
- Bye. <i>amor.</i>

2702
02:51:24.191 --> 02:51:26.276
[both speaking Spanish]

2703
02:51:30.238 --> 02:51:31.531
[Silvia speaking Spanish]

2704
02:51:31.615 --> 02:51:33.116
<i>- Adios.</i>
- [Silvia. in English] Bye.

2705
02:52:12.489 --> 02:52:15.325
[car horn honking]

2706
02:52:21.498 --> 02:52:22.541
Fifty cents.

2707
02:52:27.254 --> 02:52:28.547
[Manny. in English] Thank you.

2708
02:52:35.846 --> 02:52:38.807
[upbeat music playing]

2709
02:52:38.974 --> 02:52:42.018
<i>♪ All I do is dream of you
The whole night through ♪</i>

2710
02:52:42.853 --> 02:52:46.356
<i>♪ With the dawn I still go on
Dreaming of you ♪</i>

2711
02:52:46.773 --> 02:52:50.735
<i>♪ You're every thought. you're everything
You're every song I ever sing ♪</i>

2712
02:52:50.986 --> 02:52:54.155
<i>♪ Summer. winter. autumn. and spring ♪</i>

2713
02:52:54.489 --> 02:52:58.285
<i>♪ And were there more
Than 24 hours a day ♪</i>

2714
02:52:58.702 --> 02:53:02.372
<i>♪ They'd be spent in sweet content
Dreamin' away ♪</i>

2715
02:53:02.664 --> 02:53:06.626
<i>♪ When skies are grey. when skies are blue
Morning. noon and nighttime too ♪</i>

2716
02:53:06.793 --> 02:53:10.839
<i>♪ All I do the whole day through
Is dream of you ♪</i>

2717
02:53:18.471 --> 02:53:19.471
[upbeat music concludes]

2718
02:53:19.556 --> 02:53:20.432
[man 1]<i> Save it.</i>

2719
02:53:20.515 --> 02:53:23.035
[man 2] <i>Save it. Tell them to go home.</i>
<i>We're shutting down for a few weeks.</i>

2720
02:53:23.059 --> 02:53:24.662
- [man 1] <i>What?</i>
- [man 2] <i>Well. don't just stand there.</i>

2721
02:53:24.686 --> 02:53:26.396
<i>- Tell them.</i>
- [man 1] <i>Everybody go home</i>

2722
02:53:26.479 --> 02:53:27.879
<i>until further notice. What is this?</i>

2723
02:53:28.023 --> 02:53:29.250
[man 3] <i>Yeah. What's the matter?</i>

2724
02:53:29.274 --> 02:53:31.377
[man 2] <i>The jazz singer.</i>
<i>That's what's the matter. The jazz singer.</i>

2725
02:53:31.401 --> 02:53:35.280
<i>♪ Oh my darling little mammy
Down in Alabamy… ♪</i>

2726
02:53:35.447 --> 02:53:37.258
[man 2] <i>This is no joke. Cosmo.</i>
<i>It's a sensation.</i>

2727
02:53:37.282 --> 02:53:38.602
<i>The public is screaming for more.</i>

2728
02:53:38.742 --> 02:53:40.219
- [Cosmo]<i> More what?</i>
- [man 2] <i>Talking pictures.</i>

2729
02:53:40.243 --> 02:53:41.119
<i>Talking pictures.</i>

2730
02:53:41.244 --> 02:53:42.847
<i>- Aw. it's just a freak.
- Yeah. what a freak.</i>

2731
02:53:42.871 --> 02:53:44.432
<i>We should have such a freak
at this studio.</i>

2732
02:53:44.456 --> 02:53:47.336
<i>I told you talking pictures were a menace.
but no one would listen to me.</i>

2733
02:53:47.792 --> 02:53:49.669
<i>Don. we're gonna put
our best feet forward.</i>

2734
02:53:49.794 --> 02:53:52.505
<i>We're going to make</i> The Dueling Cavalier
<i>into a talking picture.</i>

2735
02:53:52.589 --> 02:53:54.132
[dramatic music playing]

2736
02:53:59.179 --> 02:54:02.891
[woman vocalizing in film]

2737
02:54:03.516 --> 02:54:08.063
<i>No. no. Miss Demont.
Round tones. round tones.</i>

2738
02:54:08.313 --> 02:54:10.690
<i>Now let me hear you read your line.</i>

2739
02:54:12.192 --> 02:54:14.486
<i>And I can't stand him.</i>

2740
02:54:14.986 --> 02:54:17.489
<i>Pierre. you shouldn't have come.</i>

2741
02:54:18.281 --> 02:54:20.951
<i>Pierre. you shouldn't have come.</i>

2742
02:54:21.326 --> 02:54:24.079
[man] <i>She's gotta talk into the mic.</i>
<i>I can't pick it up.</i>

2743
02:54:24.162 --> 02:54:26.748
[Miss Demont] <i>I was talking.</i>
<i>wasn't I. Miss Dinsmore?</i>

2744
02:54:26.873 --> 02:54:30.335
[Miss Dinsmore] <i>Yes. my dear.</i>
<i>but please remember round tones.</i>

2745
02:54:30.543 --> 02:54:32.170
[Miss Demont speaking faintly]

2746
02:54:32.295 --> 02:54:33.838
[gentle music playing]

2747
02:54:35.715 --> 02:54:37.634
[Miss Demont screams]

2748
02:54:39.678 --> 02:54:41.388
[audience laughing]

2749
02:54:42.597 --> 02:54:47.185
<i>I love you. I love you.
I love you. I love you.</i>

2750
02:54:55.193 --> 02:54:57.612
[man] <i>Good night. See you tomorrow.</i>

2751
02:54:57.737 --> 02:55:00.532
[woman] <i>Good night. darling.</i>
<i>Take care of that throat.</i>

2752
02:55:01.157 --> 02:55:03.284
<i>You're a big singing star now. remember?</i>

2753
02:55:04.452 --> 02:55:07.789
<i>This California dew is
just a little heavier than usual tonight.</i>

2754
02:55:07.956 --> 02:55:12.836
[man] <i>Really? Where I stand.</i>
<i>the sun is shining all over the place.</i>

2755
02:55:26.474 --> 02:55:28.643
["Singin' in the Rain" playing]

2756
02:56:02.802 --> 02:56:06.389
<i>♪ I'm singin' in the rain ♪</i>

2757
02:56:06.514 --> 02:56:09.726
<i>♪ Just singin' in the rain ♪</i>

2758
02:56:10.018 --> 02:56:13.229
<i>♪ What a glorious feeling ♪</i>

2759
02:56:13.313 --> 02:56:16.483
<i>♪ I'm happy again ♪</i>

2760
02:56:17.358 --> 02:56:19.652
<i>♪ I'm laughing at clouds ♪</i>

2761
02:56:19.861 --> 02:56:23.198
<i>♪ So dark up above ♪</i>

2762
02:56:24.157 --> 02:56:26.534
<i>♪ The sun's in my heart ♪</i>

2763
02:56:26.659 --> 02:56:29.704
<i>♪ And I'm ready for love ♪</i>

2764
02:56:30.163 --> 02:56:33.291
<i>♪ Let the stormy clouds chase ♪</i>

2765
02:56:33.750 --> 02:56:36.961
<i>♪ Everyone from the place ♪</i>

2766
02:56:38.171 --> 02:56:40.048
<i>♪ Come on with the rain ♪</i>

2767
02:56:40.131 --> 02:56:44.135
<i>♪ I've a smile on my face ♪</i>

2768
02:56:44.219 --> 02:56:47.222
<i>♪ I'll walk down the lane ♪</i>

2769
02:56:47.597 --> 02:56:51.142
<i>♪ With a happy refrain ♪</i>

2770
02:56:51.309 --> 02:56:55.897
<i>♪ Just singin'. singin' in the rain ♪</i>

2771
02:56:58.900 --> 02:57:01.486
<i>♪ Dancin' in the rain ♪</i>

2772
02:57:09.619 --> 02:57:12.038
<i>♪ I'm happy again ♪</i>

2773
02:57:12.205 --> 02:57:13.665
["Singin' in the Rain" fades]

2774
02:57:13.790 --> 02:57:17.544
[upbeat music playing]

2775
02:57:50.243 --> 02:57:51.578
[Nellie] <i>Tell me why.</i>

2776
02:57:51.703 --> 02:57:53.872
- [Manny]<i> Why?</i>
- [Nellie] <i>Yeah. tell me why.</i>

2777
02:57:54.038 --> 02:57:55.707
[Manny]<i> I don't know why.</i>

2778
02:57:56.541 --> 02:57:58.835
<i>I just want to be part
of something bigger.</i>

2779
02:57:59.085 --> 02:58:00.628
<i>To be part of something important.</i>

2780
02:58:00.712 --> 02:58:02.392
something that lasts.
that means something.

2781
02:58:28.239 --> 02:58:31.534
[upbeat music intensifies]

2782
02:58:57.227 --> 02:58:59.896
[upbeat music continues]

2783
02:59:36.641 --> 02:59:39.769
[music intensifies]

2784
03:00:18.516 --> 03:00:20.059
[upbeat music ends abruptly]

2785
03:00:32.864 --> 03:00:36.909
[musical flourish]

2786
03:00:44.083 --> 03:00:45.585
[upbeat music concludes]

2787
03:00:46.210 --> 03:00:49.047
[upbeat jazz music playing]

2788
03:04:41.070 --> 03:04:42.238
[upbeat jazz music concludes]

2789
03:04:45.491 --> 03:04:47.618
[jazzy music playing]

2790
03:07:05.506 --> 03:07:07.133
[jazz music concludes]

2791
03:07:09.218 --> 03:07:11.387
[gentle music playing]

2792
03:08:44.772 --> 03:08:46.273
[gentle music concludes]

